# Cloudflare Pages redirects, read from the output directory. One rule per line:
#   <from>  <to>  <status>
#
# A source here must be a PATH. Pages rejects an absolute-URL source outright,
# and because madcowhq.com and www.madcowhq.com are both attached to the same
# Pages project, nothing in this file can tell the two hosts apart.
#
# So the www -> apex redirect is NOT here. It is a Redirect Rule on the
# madcowhq.com zone, named "www to apex (301)", recorded in README.md under
# Hosting. The direction - www to the apex, not the reverse - was picked
# because the apex is what goes on a resume and in an App Store listing, and a
# bare domain is shorter to say out loud.
#
# This file held that rule as an absolute-URL source from 2026-08-21 to
# 2026-08-23. It never fired. Every deploy logged
#   "Parsed 0 valid redirect rules. Found invalid redirect lines: ... Only
#    relative URLs are allowed."
# and then reported success, so www served a duplicate of the whole site.
#
# Deliberately absent: the 301 from madcowhq.com/sailing. Nothing links there,
# and epic #1 puts it out of scope until something does. That one WOULD belong
# in this file - it is a path redirect within one host.
#
# Add path redirects below, sources beginning with "/".
#
# /apps/ folded into /work/ (#81). EXACT paths only - no splat - so that
# /apps/taskr/ and its support and privacy pages keep serving, and any other
# missing /apps/<x>/ falls through to whatever Pages does with a missing path
# (#36 makes that a 404) instead of landing on /work/.
#
# The second and third lines are each needed: under `wrangler pages dev` with
# the first line alone, /apps and /apps/index.html both answered 200 with no
# Location (wrangler 4.131.2, 2026-09-14; the runs are in #81's PR).
/apps/  /work/  301
/apps  /work/  301
/apps/index.html  /work/  301
